From 292bfe59243af32e1791bcec019f758672bc64f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Aug 2021 14:17:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 009/572] feat(stm32mp2): manage core 1 enabling

After boot, the BootROM will issue a reset of the Cortex-A35 cores.
Core 0 will boot till kernel. Core 1 is placed in WFI in TF-A BL2.
Through PSCI, Linux will ask to have Core 1 available. The PSCI platform
code is done in stm32_pwr_domain_on(). Core0 will change Core1 reset
address thanks to CA35SS_SYSCFG_VBAR_CR register to BL31 entry point.
And will reset Core1 by setting RCC_C1P1RSTCSETR_C1P1PORRST bit.
It is possible to turn core 1 on and off. But it is not possible to do
so on core 0.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 27370be05e545e54a9c63684981002729c11ba1d feat(stm32mp2): manage core 1 enabling]
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: I01e59e3a2398c48cc050ec4703d6610da9e9c4bd
---
 plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c | 101 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 94 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c b/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c
index 9be42c59c7..613f08f154 100644
--- a/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c
+++ b/plat/st/stm32mp2/stm32mp2_pm.c
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 /*
- * Copyright (c) 2024, STMicroelectronics - All Rights Reserved
+ * Copyright (c) 2024-2026, STMicroelectronics - All Rights Reserved
